shine shine shine

531
00:22:29,717 --> 00:22:31,952
♪ Shine shine shine shine

532
00:22:31,985 --> 00:22:34,153
- How are ya?
- I'm peaking.

533
00:22:34,755 --> 00:22:37,390
♪ Baby just shine
shine shine shine

534
00:22:37,423 --> 00:22:39,927
♪ Shine shine shine shine

535
00:22:39,960 --> 00:22:42,995
You know,
I buffed my love once,

536
00:22:43,028 --> 00:22:45,965
I never shined it.

537
00:22:49,202 --> 00:22:51,103
Next on Don
Kirshner's Rock Concert,

538
00:22:51,137 --> 00:22:53,940
one of the greatest
influences on the disco scene

539
00:22:53,973 --> 00:22:56,042
of the late 70's.

540
00:22:56,308 --> 00:22:59,045
She's leaving, yay! Woo!

541
00:23:01,648 --> 00:23:02,882
Now she's got one of those.

542
00:23:02,915 --> 00:23:04,417
Oh, hmm.

543
00:23:04,985 --> 00:23:06,987
We've never seen
such great disco.

544
00:23:08,455 --> 00:23:10,057
Thank you,
thank you very much.

545
00:23:10,090 --> 00:23:12,325
As most of you know,
this is my closing show

546
00:23:12,358 --> 00:23:14,327
of this engagement,
and there's somebody

547
00:23:14,360 --> 00:23:16,597
in the audience, I'm sure
you'd all like to meet.

548
00:23:16,630 --> 00:23:17,930
The guy who cancelled me.

549
00:23:17,963 --> 00:23:19,432
One of the living
legends of show business,

550
00:23:19,465 --> 00:23:21,435
Mr. Arthur Godfrey.

551
00:23:21,468 --> 00:23:23,637
(applause)

552
00:23:24,570 --> 00:23:25,905
Thank you, you're all fired.

553
00:23:25,938 --> 00:23:28,775
You have no humility,
all of you.

554
00:23:30,277 --> 00:23:31,277
(belches)

555
00:23:36,048 --> 00:23:37,383
You've been a
wonderful audience,

556
00:23:37,417 --> 00:23:39,118
and as always Las
Vegas is the best

557
00:23:39,152 --> 00:23:41,053
place in the world to entertain.

558
00:23:41,087 --> 00:23:42,388
Thank you.

559
00:23:42,422 --> 00:23:44,958
(doors close)

560
00:23:53,800 --> 00:23:55,335
Okay, everybody.

561
00:23:55,368 --> 00:23:56,737
In the spirit of the 70's,

562
00:23:56,770 --> 00:23:59,338
I've come up with a
brilliant Blaxploitation film

563
00:23:59,372 --> 00:24:00,973
for all of us to star in.

564
00:24:01,007 --> 00:24:03,075
Crow, I don't know,
it just seems to me that

565
00:24:03,108 --> 00:24:05,078
you've reworked
"Earth Vs. Soup"

566
00:24:05,112 --> 00:24:07,013
and inserted jivy
character names.

567
00:24:07,047 --> 00:24:08,282
Like I'm that lazy.

568
00:24:08,315 --> 00:24:10,083
Now, I'm confused.

569
00:24:10,117 --> 00:24:12,052
Am I Chocolate Jones
or Sugar Fly McQueen?

570
00:24:12,085 --> 00:24:13,887
Uh, you're both
and you're also

571
00:24:13,920 --> 00:24:16,088
reading the part of
Sweet Mama String Bean

572
00:24:16,122 --> 00:24:18,225
who runs the boutique de beaute.

573
00:24:18,258 --> 00:24:20,927
Okay Mike, uh,
let's see, take it from...

574
00:24:20,960 --> 00:24:24,030
Afro's and Bafro's line
on the top of page five.

575
00:24:24,063 --> 00:24:25,998
Okay,

576
00:24:26,032 --> 00:24:28,335
Girl, don't think
on soul brothers.

577
00:24:28,368 --> 00:24:29,870
I don't have any lines.

578
00:24:29,903 --> 00:24:32,005
Well, but you get to
wear slinky dresses,

579
00:24:32,038 --> 00:24:33,740
and hold guns and stuff.

580
00:24:33,773 --> 00:24:35,375
Not this sister!

581
00:24:35,408 --> 00:24:37,410
Crow, you know, I don't
know how to tell you this

582
00:24:37,443 --> 00:24:39,045
but uh, I mean, look at me.

583
00:24:39,078 --> 00:24:40,780
I'm really not that funky.

584
00:24:40,813 --> 00:24:43,617
Mike, to me you're the
Don Cornelius of the 90's.

585
00:24:43,650 --> 00:24:46,118
Well, I don't really
see it that way.

586
00:24:46,152 --> 00:24:47,953
"Chocolate Jones and
the Temple of Funk"

587
00:24:47,987 --> 00:24:49,555
is guaranteed boffo box office.

588
00:24:49,588 --> 00:24:52,992
Smudgey the Bootblack,
which is of course, my part.

589
00:24:53,025 --> 00:24:54,727
So I'll need a cane.

590
00:24:54,760 --> 00:24:57,197
Oh and Mike, what size
dashiki do you wear?

591
00:24:57,230 --> 00:24:59,098
Well, I'll get a large.

592
00:24:59,132 --> 00:25:00,500
Now, the Cadillacs.

593
00:25:01,167 --> 00:25:03,303
(theme music)

594
00:25:06,105 --> 00:25:06,907
(sighs)

595
00:25:06,940 --> 00:25:08,107
(knock at door)

596
00:25:08,140 --> 00:25:09,008
Come in.

597
00:25:09,042 --> 00:25:10,010
Where'd you go?

598
00:25:10,043 --> 00:25:13,880
Mr. Godfrey, I'm
so glad you came by.

599
00:25:13,913 --> 00:25:15,615
How are ya,
how are ya, how are ya?

600
00:25:15,948 --> 00:25:17,783
I just came to say thank you

601
00:25:17,817 --> 00:25:19,352
for that wonderful introduction.

602
00:25:19,385 --> 00:25:21,120
That was very kind of you,

603
00:25:21,153 --> 00:25:22,388
and I had to come
back and tell you,

604
00:25:22,422 --> 00:25:25,025
you were great, wonderful.

605
00:25:25,058 --> 00:25:26,993
Michelle, you're just starting.

606
00:25:27,027 --> 00:25:28,528
You can have anything you want,

607
00:25:28,562 --> 00:25:30,763
TV, movies, anything.

608
00:25:30,797 --> 00:25:34,067
You have the makings
of a superstar,

609
00:25:34,100 --> 00:25:35,335
and I've invited all the stars

610
00:25:35,368 --> 00:25:38,070
that are playing Vegas this
week to come to my suite

611
00:25:38,103 --> 00:25:39,907
about three o'clock
in the morning

612
00:25:39,940 --> 00:25:41,173
for a little get together.

613
00:25:41,207 --> 00:25:43,042
I'd love to have you come.

614
00:25:43,075 --> 00:25:44,543
Can you make it?

615
00:25:44,577 --> 00:25:47,013
Oh, I'd love to but
I'm doing LA tomorrow.

616
00:25:47,047 --> 00:25:49,015
Get out of my dressing room.

617
00:25:49,048 --> 00:25:50,783
I'd love to have
you but I understand.

618
00:25:50,817 --> 00:25:52,718
Your career comes
first, of course.

619
00:25:52,752 --> 00:25:56,522
You keep straight like that
and you will be a star.

620
00:25:56,555 --> 00:25:59,092
Thank you Mr. G-- Arthur.

621
00:25:59,125 --> 00:26:01,828
Come on over here, how
about a little co-host.

622
00:26:01,862 --> 00:26:03,797
(grunts)

623
00:26:05,132 --> 00:26:06,298
Thank you.

624
00:26:07,233 --> 00:26:09,735
Take the wheel, Skipper.

625
00:26:09,768 --> 00:26:10,470
Hey sweetheart,

626
00:26:11,705 --> 00:26:12,905
I got us booked again
for The Carson Show.

627
00:26:12,938 --> 00:26:15,075
Everything's going to
start happening for us.

628
00:26:15,108 --> 00:26:17,177
All that work that you've
worked so hard for,

629
00:26:17,210 --> 00:26:18,177
it's gonna all start paying off.

630
00:26:18,210 --> 00:26:19,845
Nothing can stop us.

631
00:26:19,878 --> 00:26:21,380
And with your record on the
charts and still climbing,

632
00:26:21,413 --> 00:26:22,282
we're hot!

633
00:26:22,315 --> 00:26:23,850
I mean, like sizzle.

634
00:26:23,883 --> 00:26:26,953
Yes, but right now all
I want to do is change,

635
00:26:26,987 --> 00:26:29,188
and get on that plane for home.

636
00:26:29,222 --> 00:26:30,990
(phone rings)

637
00:26:32,358 --> 00:26:33,660
Shining your love?

638
00:26:33,693 --> 00:26:35,095
Hello.

639
00:26:35,128 --> 00:26:36,495
You want me to be a greeter?

640
00:26:36,528 --> 00:26:38,230
Look, don't bother her
with phone calls now.

641
00:26:38,263 --> 00:26:41,433
No, I will not call
you little buddy.

642
00:26:41,467 --> 00:26:43,370
Oh...

643
00:26:43,403 --> 00:26:45,072
He looks a lot
like Gertrude Stein.

644
00:26:45,105 --> 00:26:46,873
You better take this one.

645
00:26:47,373 --> 00:26:49,175
Hello? This is
Michelle Wilson.

646
00:26:49,208 --> 00:26:51,043
Oh that's sick, Mr. Godfrey!

647
00:26:51,077 --> 00:26:53,278
Oh my god, not Bobby!

648
00:26:53,313 --> 00:26:55,115
Is he alright?

649
00:26:55,148 --> 00:26:57,117
Oh, no.

650
00:26:57,150 --> 00:26:58,785
He is alright.

651
00:27:01,955 --> 00:27:04,123
Three fountains in a fountain.

652
00:27:05,225 --> 00:27:06,058
We're lucky.

653
00:27:06,092 --> 00:27:07,260
We have a three seater bidet.

654
00:27:07,293 --> 00:27:09,028
I'll pay all
expenses, everything.

655
00:27:09,062 --> 00:27:11,397
He's practicing to
be on Mike Douglas.

656
00:27:11,430 --> 00:27:13,098
So just take a
couple of weeks off.

657
00:27:13,132 --> 00:27:16,970
Relax, that way you can go
see Bobby in the hospital

658
00:27:17,003 --> 00:27:17,870
and--

659
00:27:17,903 --> 00:27:19,072
I almost called you Gilligan.

660
00:27:19,072 --> 00:27:21,573
Well, then you'll see,
he'll be home in no time.

661
00:27:23,877 --> 00:27:26,078
Its Fran Lebowitz,
still not writing.

662
00:27:26,112 --> 00:27:27,480
Excuse me Miss
Wilson, a Miss Thomas

663
00:27:27,513 --> 00:27:29,082
is here to see you.

664
00:27:29,115 --> 00:27:31,083
She say to tell you, she's
Bobby's schoolteacher.

665
00:27:31,117 --> 00:27:33,018
And can he get her any pot?

666
00:27:33,085 --> 00:27:35,022
Show her in, please.

667
00:27:35,055 --> 00:27:36,055
It's the colorful domestic

668
00:27:36,088 --> 00:27:38,123
who adds all the
humor to the show.

669
00:27:41,093 --> 00:27:42,028
Welcome to Skipper's,

670
00:27:42,062 --> 00:27:43,897
maybe you'd like
to wait in the bar.

671
00:27:43,930 --> 00:27:47,033
Michelle, I'll
leave you two alone.

672
00:27:47,067 --> 00:27:48,902
Now if you need anything, call.

673
00:27:48,935 --> 00:27:50,870
Day or night, anything.

674
00:27:50,903 --> 00:27:52,072
Pardon me.

675
00:27:52,105 --> 00:27:52,905
What would you possibly need

676
00:27:52,938 --> 00:27:54,540
from an Alan Hale Jr.?

677
00:27:54,573 --> 00:27:55,908
I don't know.

678
00:27:55,942 --> 00:27:58,310
I'm awfully sorry about
Bobby, he's a fine boy.

679
00:27:58,343 --> 00:28:00,480
Nobody deserves a
beating like that.

680
00:28:00,513 --> 00:28:01,848
Pauly Shore does.

681
00:28:01,882 --> 00:28:03,683
He wouldn't even tell
me who beat him up.

682
00:28:04,450 --> 00:28:07,387
The doctor said
he was on drugs.

683
00:28:07,420 --> 00:28:08,922
How am I related
to him, again?

684
00:28:08,955 --> 00:28:10,923
God, I didn't even know
he was using this stuff.

685
00:28:10,957 --> 00:28:12,792
He also made an
attempt on Ford's life.

686
00:28:12,825 --> 00:28:14,060
He's so young.

687
00:28:14,093 --> 00:28:16,128
Bobby's lucky, he'll be okay.

688
00:28:16,162 --> 00:28:17,797
Some kids aren't as lucky.

689
00:28:17,830 --> 00:28:19,565
I shouldn't have left him
with just the housekeeper.

690
00:28:19,598 --> 00:28:23,002
I'm talking about the men who
push poison onto young kids.

691
00:28:23,035 --> 00:28:24,870
Something's gotta
be done to stop it.

692
00:28:24,903 --> 00:28:26,873
very day a new drug comes along,

693
00:28:26,907 --> 00:28:29,175
and these creeps
push it onto kids.

694
00:28:29,208 --> 00:28:31,243
Every day?
That's good marketing.

695
00:28:31,277 --> 00:28:34,013
I've got something
in here for you to see.

696
00:28:34,047 --> 00:28:35,982
This is very interesting
and I've got it

697
00:28:36,015 --> 00:28:37,483
in a very important place.

698
00:28:37,517 --> 00:28:38,685
It's got wings.

699
00:28:38,718 --> 00:28:40,052
It's in here, I
know it is, someplace.

700
00:28:40,087 --> 00:28:41,153
It's really important.

701
00:28:41,187 --> 00:28:43,990
I know I've got it in
here, now, just a moment.

702
00:28:44,023 --> 00:28:45,092
Oh, heck!

703
00:28:45,125 --> 00:28:46,658
Oh wait,

704
00:28:46,692 --> 00:28:48,628
Here's a Velamints stuck
to a Kleenex, want it?

705
00:28:48,662 --> 00:28:50,697
Ah, here it is.

706
00:28:50,730 --> 00:28:52,898
I'm taking a big chance
showing you this.

707
00:28:52,932 --> 00:28:54,967
A map of historic
Williamsburg.

708
00:28:55,000 --> 00:28:57,470
I've been working on
this for over two years.

709
00:28:57,503 --> 00:29:00,907
This is an area located about
75 miles east of Los Angeles.

710
00:29:00,940 --> 00:29:03,042
Nearest town is
over 20 miles away.

711
00:29:03,075 --> 00:29:04,010
You're booked there.

712
00:29:04,043 --> 00:29:05,145
This is where
they take the stuff

713
00:29:05,178 --> 00:29:06,745
that comes in from overseas,

714
00:29:06,780 --> 00:29:09,415
and process it down to what
they sell on the street.

715
00:29:09,448 --> 00:29:11,050
There's millions of
dollars worth of drugs

716
00:29:11,083 --> 00:29:13,018
being processed
in this building.

717
00:29:13,052 --> 00:29:14,353
Mmhmm.

718
00:29:14,387 --> 00:29:15,922
Much of it highly
explosive chemicals.

719
00:29:16,588 --> 00:29:18,858
We can destroy it in
less than a minute,

720
00:29:18,892 --> 00:29:20,793
and I know the people
who can help us.

721
00:29:20,827 --> 00:29:22,795
But I can't approach them,
they don't know me,

722
00:29:22,828 --> 00:29:24,297
would never trust me.

723
00:29:24,330 --> 00:29:26,565
But since your song
is doing so well,

724
00:29:26,598 --> 00:29:27,900
and they know who you are--

725
00:29:27,933 --> 00:29:29,902
Fame equals trustworthy.

726
00:29:29,935 --> 00:29:30,970
Maybe we can
approach them together.

727
00:29:31,003 --> 00:29:32,972
What? I wasn't listening.

728
00:29:33,005 --> 00:29:34,973
You really think that
we can pull this off?

729
00:29:35,007 --> 00:29:36,977
Oh yes, I'm positive!

730
00:29:37,010 --> 00:29:39,178
I'm a very organized person,

731
00:29:39,212 --> 00:29:41,247
and this map is perfect
in every detail.

732
00:29:41,280 --> 00:29:43,517
I know we can do it.

733
00:29:43,550 --> 00:29:45,083
Women can make a difference.

734
00:29:45,117 --> 00:29:48,087
Ah, the director wrote
that so he could get laid.

735
00:29:48,120 --> 00:29:49,922
(gun shots)

736
00:29:53,893 --> 00:29:55,828
Fantastic, cut.

737
00:29:55,862 --> 00:29:57,530
Clean up the corpse,
let's move on.

738
00:29:57,563 --> 00:29:58,898
Barry Knight's first feature.

739
00:29:58,932 --> 00:29:59,898
(chuckles)

740
00:29:59,932 --> 00:30:00,900
You alright?

741
00:30:00,933 --> 00:30:01,868
Sure, no sweat, it was a snap.

742
00:30:01,902 --> 00:30:02,868
Did you get it, I hope?

743
00:30:02,902 --> 00:30:04,070
Yeah, I think so.

744
00:30:04,103 --> 00:30:04,970
How'd it look?

745
00:30:05,003 --> 00:30:06,072
Terrific.

746
00:30:06,105 --> 00:30:06,907
Should we have filmed it?

747
00:30:06,940 --> 00:30:07,907
That's good, you can go now.

748
00:30:07,940 --> 00:30:09,908
Let's get a real
actor in here please.

749
00:30:09,942 --> 00:30:11,043
Uh, that'll blow
the budget sir.

750
00:30:11,077 --> 00:30:12,978
Come on Rick, hurry up
with the actor, would ya?

751
00:30:13,012 --> 00:30:14,913
Jesus, would you
please take your mark?

752
00:30:14,947 --> 00:30:16,582
Come on, could
we get an actor?

753
00:30:17,350 --> 00:30:19,018
Jeez.

754
00:30:19,052 --> 00:30:21,253
Her name's Terri Grant,
she's the best stunt driver

755
00:30:21,287 --> 00:30:22,088
in Hollywood.

756
00:30:22,122 --> 00:30:23,488
And she's deaf.

757
00:30:23,523 --> 00:30:25,258
She can drive and
modify a vehicle better

758
00:30:25,292 --> 00:30:27,393
than anyone else in this town.

759
00:30:27,427 --> 00:30:30,830
She'll help us, her brother
overdosed five years ago.

760
00:30:30,863 --> 00:30:31,830
She's black you know.

761
00:30:31,865 --> 00:30:33,533
Oh, um, Miss Grant!

762
00:30:34,000 --> 00:30:37,003
That was a fantastic
stunt, are you okay?

763
00:30:37,037 --> 00:30:38,303
Oh sure, thanks.

764
00:30:38,337 --> 00:30:39,705
We need a real stunt sign!

765
00:30:39,738 --> 00:30:40,973
Nothing to it if you
know what you're doing.

766
00:30:41,007 --> 00:30:42,375
Hey, you're Michelle
Wilson, aren't you?

767
00:30:42,408 --> 00:30:43,375
You're terrible.

768
00:30:43,408 --> 00:30:44,843
God, I just love your voice.

769
00:30:44,877 --> 00:30:45,978
Are you working on this movie?

770
00:30:46,012 --> 00:30:49,015
No, but we've got something
to talk to you about,

771
00:30:49,048 --> 00:30:50,048
It's about the pencil test.

772
00:30:50,082 --> 00:30:51,918
and it's not making movies.

773
00:30:52,718 --> 00:30:54,220
So come on in, we'll talk.

774
00:30:54,853 --> 00:30:56,890
Do you have a stunt
bra for my friend?

775
00:30:57,690 --> 00:30:58,992
Ya!

776
00:30:59,025 --> 00:30:59,958
That's Keiko Yumaro,
here from Vietnam

777
00:30:59,992 --> 00:31:01,227
a little over two years,

778
00:31:01,260 --> 00:31:03,462
and knows what problems
kids can get into.

779
00:31:03,495 --> 00:31:05,865
She teaches karate and
dance for these kids

780
00:31:05,898 --> 00:31:06,865
in the morning.

781
00:31:06,900 --> 00:31:07,900
She'll help.

782
00:31:07,933 --> 00:31:09,302
She's the Asian
one in our group.

783
00:31:09,335 --> 00:31:10,837
Ya!

784
00:31:10,870 --> 00:31:11,972
You killed my
brother last week

785
00:31:12,005 --> 00:31:13,640
Ya, ya!

786
00:31:13,673 --> 00:31:14,973
Can we go?

787
00:31:15,007 --> 00:31:17,510
Ya, ya, ya!

788
00:31:17,543 --> 00:31:19,778
A very special,
All-American girl.

789
00:31:22,015 --> 00:31:24,283
La Choy makes Chinese food.

790
00:31:26,518 --> 00:31:27,053
Get her!

791
00:31:27,087 --> 00:31:27,820
Rip her apart!

792
00:31:27,853 --> 00:31:28,755
Kill her!

793
00:31:28,788 --> 00:31:30,623
(kids cheer)

794
00:31:31,958 --> 00:31:33,092
Darn it!

795
00:31:33,125 --> 00:31:35,462
Now I know it's in
here somewhere.

796
00:31:35,495 --> 00:31:37,997
I just know it, I
put it here myself.

797
00:31:38,030 --> 00:31:39,798
Oh,

798
00:31:39,832 --> 00:31:41,467
Oh, Popeye.

799
00:31:41,500 --> 00:31:43,002
Here it is, oh good.

800
00:31:43,035 --> 00:31:45,705
Okay, are you ready?

801
00:31:46,405 --> 00:31:49,075
Do you think you could climb
to the roof of that building

802
00:31:49,108 --> 00:31:51,077
